        "original_id": "26c46a71-5fb3-5835-b152-0e47a11a7ac0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Holdstock, H. L. Mencken\n- Works: Mythago Wood\n- Roles: Novelist, author, journalist, satirist, cultural critic, scholar\n- Topics: Fantasy literature, mythic fiction, American English\n\nFacts:\n- H. L. Mencken was born on September 12, 1880, and he was an American journalist, satirist, cultural critic, and scholar of American English.\n- Robert Holdstock was born on August 2, 1948, and he was an English novelist and author.\n- Mythago Wood is a fantasy novel by British writer Robert Holdstock, and it was published in the United Kingdom in 1984.\n- Robert Holdstock was best known for works of Celtic, Nordic, Gothic, and Pictish fantasy literature, predominantly in the fantasy subgenre of mythic fiction.\n- H. L. Mencken died on January 29, 1956.\n- Robert Holdstock died on November 29, 2009.",
